  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0263df275083eba45b37ab9636c8dcbf, type: 3}
  m_Name: MAP-068_Whiteout
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  mapId: MAP-068
  displayName: Whiteout
  environment: Arctic / Snow
  warfareFocus: Visibility, Thermal Sensors, Navigation
  executiveSummary: A snow-choked Arctic battlefield built for visibility-degraded combat, thermal-sensor warfare, and hazardous navigation. Features blizzard corridors, ice dunes, frozen ravines, research shelters, buried communications towers, and wind-carved ridges. Emphasizes autonomous navigation under near-zero visibility, thermal-sensor fusion, relay warfare, and logistics under severe Arctic conditions.
  designGoals:
  - name: Visibility-Degraded Warfare
    description: Blizzards, drifting snow, and ice fog reduce sightlines to a few meters. Units rely heavily on thermal sensors and autonomous pathfinding.
  - name: Thermal-Sensor Dominance
    description: Heat signatures become the primary detection method. Ice ridges, snow berms, and geothermal vents distort thermal readings, creating deceptive pockets.
  - name: Autonomy and Hazard Navigation
    description: Autonomous units choose routes based on wind exposure, ice stability, thermal cover, and sensor clarity. Units avoid whiteout corridors unless strategically necessary.
  - name: Sensor and Information Warfare
    description: Blizzards, ice fog, thermal distortion, and magnetic interference degrade sensors. Ridge relay towers restore clarity; destroying them creates blind pockets across the snowfields.
  - name: Logistics and Resources
    description: Fuel caches, heated shelters, and research stations provide resupply. Convoys must navigate unstable ice and avoid ambush-prone snow corridors.
  - name: Deployment and Progress
    description: Approximately 10000 deployment points. Players choose between thermal-optimized infantry, Arctic drones, or heavy snow-capable armor. Blue deploys from the southwest snowfield camp; Red deploys from the northeast ridge shelter.
  deployment: 'Budget: approximately 10000 points. Blue: southwest snowfield camp and Arctic staging. Red: northeast ridge shelter and thermal defenses. Neutral forward outpost at (500,950) for drone resupply.'
  ar:
    viewingDistance: 4-5 m
    physicalArea: 10x10 m
    representedArea: Approximately 1 km2
    scale: 1:100
    fov: 53 degrees diagonal
    resolution: 1920x1080 per eye
    tracking: Inside-out horizontal-plane tracking; depth mesh if available; minimal real-world occlusion assumed
    interaction: Phone pointer for pan and zoom; HUD as screen-space widgets
  coordinateSystem: 1000x1000 grid; approximately 1 unit = 1 m. Origin (0,0) is the southwest corner.
  keyLocations:
  - name: Blue HQ - Snowfield Camp
    coordinate: (0,0)
    sizeOrElevation: 150x150 m
    description: Snow berms, heated tents, drone pads, and Arctic staging.
  - name: Red HQ - Ridge Shelter Command
    coordinate: (1000,1000)
    sizeOrElevation: 150x150 m
    description: Heated bunker with radar mast and thermal relays.
  - name: Central Whiteout Basin
    coordinate: (500,450)
    sizeOrElevation: 300x300 m
    description: Blizzard epicenter with near-zero visibility, unstable ice, and thermal distortion.
  - name: Research Shelter Cluster
    coordinate: (250,800)
    sizeOrElevation: 120x120 m
    description: Labs, generators, thermal shelters, and interior combat.
  - name: Ice Ridge Network
    coordinate: (800,300)
    sizeOrElevation: 200x200 m
    description: Wind-carved ridges, snow tunnels, and flanking routes.
  - name: Blizzard Corridor
    coordinate: (0,450) to (400,900)
    sizeOrElevation: Severe whiteout zone
    description: Extreme visibility loss and sensor degradation.
  - name: Frozen Trail Route
    coordinate: (300,0) to (450,350)
    sizeOrElevation: Safer but slow route
    description: Ice cracks and wind exposure.
  - name: Thermal Relay A
    coordinate: (650,150)
    sizeOrElevation: +240 m
    description: Long-range sensor vantage point with approximately 300 m coverage.
  - name: Thermal Relay B
    coordinate: (150,650)
    sizeOrElevation: +260 m
    description: Communications relay hub and geothermal control node.
  - name: Neutral Forward Outpost
    coordinate: (500,950)
    sizeOrElevation: Forward resupply zone
    description: Drone resupply zone.
  chokepointsAndSightlines:
  - name: Blizzard Corridor
    description: Severe visibility loss; ideal for stealth ambushes and thermal deception.
  - name: Ice Ridge Network
    description: Interior flanking routes with unpredictable cover due to drifting snow.
  - name: Whiteout Basin
    description: Unstable terrain, long-range thermal engagements, and environmental hazards.
  - name: Frozen Trail Route
    description: Predictable but safer route, vulnerable to overwatch from ridges.
  - name: Sightlines
    description: Thermal Relay A provides approximately 300 m sensor coverage. Blizzards and ice fog create fog-of-war pockets.
  terrain: Ice ridges, snow dunes, frozen lakes, blizzard corridors, and research shelters.
  vegetation: None; Arctic tundra only.
  buildingsAndProps: 'Military: radar dishes, thermal relays, bunkers. Industrial: generators, pipelines, research shelters. Logistics: trucks, crates, fuel drums, and drones.'
  effects: Snowstorms, ice fog, wind gusts, and thermal distortion.
  audio: Wind, cracking ice, distant machinery, and radio chatter.
  lodBudget:
  - category: Ice Ridges/Terrain
    count: 3
    trianglesPerItem: 200000
    totalTriangles: 600000
  - category: Shelters/Industrial
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 80000
    totalTriangles: 320000
  - category: Buildings/Research
    count: 15
    trianglesPerItem: 50000
    totalTriangles: 750000
  - category: Roads/Paths
    count: 4
    trianglesPerItem: 30000
    totalTriangles: 120000
  - category: Props
    count: 50
    trianglesPerItem: 10000
    totalTriangles: 500000
  textureBudget: 2048x2048 terrain/buildings; 1024x1024 props. DXT1/5 compression. Target 100 MB or less.
  engineAndPlugins: 'Source specification: Unreal ARTemplate and Nreal SDK (XREAL), with ARKit/ARCore enabled. This asset is being added to the existing Unity map database.'
  rendering: 'Source specification: forward renderer, stationary lights, baked GI, and aggressive culling.'
  anchors: Single spatial anchor for the entire map.
  interaction: Phone pointer for pan and zoom; HUD as screen-space widgets.
  multiplayer: Client-server architecture; offload AI and physics to server.
  milestones:
  - name: Month 1 - Prototype Layout
    description: Block out the whiteout basin, ridge network, research shelters, and test the AR anchor.
  - name: Month 2 - Core Systems
    description: Implement navigation mesh, cold-weather autonomy behaviors, and thermal logic.
  - name: Month 3 - AR Integration
    description: Implement anchors, plane detection, and basic interactivity.
  - name: Months 4-5 - Content Fill
    description: Create final models, textures, lighting, and audio.
  - name: Months 6-7 - Gameplay and Polish
    description: Implement objectives, balance, snowstorms, ice fog, and thermal-distortion effects.
  - name: Month 8 - Testing and QA
    description: Conduct multiplayer stress tests and sensor validation.
  testing:
  - name: Autonomy
    description: Verify cold-weather navigation, thermal-sensor logic, and hazard avoidance.
  - name: Communications and Sensors
    description: Test relay destruction, fog-of-war updates, and line-of-sight checks under blizzard conditions.
  - name: Performance
    description: Target at least 60 Hz AR rendering on the target device.
  - name: QA Checklist
    description: Test navigation, thermal logic, deployment budget enforcement, anchor drift, and sensor accuracy.
